            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for ancient times, then the Mandarin for modern times."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 想起",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "想起 — xiǎngqǐ — \"to think of; to call to mind\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "我突然想起了他的信 wǒ tūrán xiǎngqǐ le tā de xìn — I suddenly remembered his letter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two third tones meet in this word: xiǎng is said with a rising tone before qǐ, and the spelling keeps both marks."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "想起 (xiǎngqǐ) is built from 想 'to think' and 起 'to rise', both inherited from Middle Chinese, sjangX and khiX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'to think' and the second 'to rise'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
